From: pseudo <cdodge@pseudoseed.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 23:53:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] [Spec 250][Phase: phase_7] docs: re-shoot the tree with
 the project level, the role marker and a muted orphan group
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The same three widths, re-taken after the architect's review. What changed on
screen: a project heading with the project's own favicon replaces the project
name repeated on all eight cards, architect rows are captioned "Architect" in
the slot that label vacated, and the orphan group wears Settled's muted
treatment instead of amber.

The `-tree` shots are now taken at the same WIDTH in a tall window. The sidebar
scrolls under a sticky footer, so the previous pair cut the orphan group's reason
line — the last thing in the list and the one a reviewer most needs to read. The
width is what the responsive claim is about; the height is only so the picture is
complete.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
